\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3.1}{\textit {M.\,tuberculosis} variants surviving the false-negative filtering process, broken down by drug and locus. For every variant the table reports its false-negative (FN) prevalence and the proportion of resistant (R) samples in which the variant was absent. FN\,=\,false negative; R\,=\,resistant; ---\,=\,no relevant variant detected. Variants are written as \texttt {position\,REF}$\rightarrow $\texttt {ALT}.}}{36}{table.3.1}%
